      "local_reason_code": "cloud_cluster_control_not_applicable",
      "local_deviation": "Cluster and ACP runner-pool administration remain visible as a native route contract in Local mode but require Cloud authority; registration tokens are never synthesized or cached by the renderer.",
      "judgment_rationale": "Cluster list and detail pages are direct sources for the canonical cluster control plane. Reads require tenant membership while cluster create, update, delete, ACP runner-pool creation, and registration-token actions require tenant administration; the uncalled runner-pool update service method is not surface authority, and no cluster:read permission exists. Cloud Desktop now implements a native tenant-member slice with paginated list reads, current-page search and status filtering, refresh, and health inspection. It does not expose cluster detail, mutations, ACP runner-pool management, or registration-token authority, and its strict client projection discards encrypted credentials, Provider configuration, and token fields. Local Desktop keeps the native route shell but returns the stable not-applicable authority instead of simulating a cluster topology.",
